_private/
_system/trading/portfolio_hub/.env

# Research Watchdog: the ranked report names held positions and their market
# values. This repository is public, and no committed artifact has ever carried
# real account values (darwin_portfolio*.json are model weights). Only the
# redacted receipt at _system/data/research_watchdog_receipt.json is committed.
_system/data/research_watchdog.json
_system/reviews/WATCHDOG.md

# Raw SEC filings are a CACHE of a free, permanent, public archive (EDGAR), not
# authored content. Measured 2026-09-07: 32.8 GB across 573 tickers / 36,470
# .htm files -- ~95% of this repo's bytes and 0% of its analysis. Git stores
# every version forever and 11 MB inline-XBRL documents barely delta-compress,
# so this content is what drove .git to ~19 GB and is why large pushes 408.
#
# The committed artifact is the POINTER, never the payload: each ticker's
# investor-documents/DOWNLOAD_MANIFEST.json records the form, accession, primary
# document and sec.gov URL of every filing (11.7 MB for the entire corpus, vs
# 32.8 GB of payload), and research/evidence/sec_companyfacts.json carries the
# structured XBRL facts. Any ticker rehydrates in ~30s with
# `python _system/scripts/download_us_investor_docs.py --ticker <T>`.
#
# Same rule already applied to _system/graph/graph.db and research/evidence/_text/.
# NOTE: this stops future growth only. Filings committed before this rule remain
# tracked; removing them from history needs a coordinated git-filter-repo pass.
# IR PDFs (investor-documents/ir-*) are deliberately NOT ignored -- IR sites
# rotate and 404, so those are not reliably re-fetchable.
*/investor-documents/sec-edgar/
